{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tired-stonebroke-sable","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# A — PreToolUse hook: re-surface Serena on every grep\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`AGENTS.md` already says to prefer Serena's symbol tools over `grep`, and an agent with Serena configured still\nenumerated call sites by hand with `grep` for many turns (epic `061c` story S2). Launch-time guidance decays: by\nmid-task, one line of a long document has no salience. The fix is a reminder delivered **at the moment of the\naction**, executed by the harness rather than remembered by the agent.\n\n## Approach\n\nA `PreToolUse` hook on the `Bash` tool that emits a short reminder when the command invokes the grep family.\n\n**The trigger must be as dumb as possible.** Match a grep-family invocation (`grep`, `rg`, `egrep`, `fgrep`) in\nthe command string — nothing more. Deliberately do NOT try to classify whether the pattern \"looks like a\nsymbol\", whether the target is under `src/`, or parse the command: a clever predicate is fragile, mis-fires, and\na hook that mis-fires gets disabled, which is worse than a hook that occasionally reminds you of something you\nalready knew. Accepting false positives is the design, because the cost of a false positive is three lines of\ntext and the cost of a false negative is the behaviour this epic exists to fix.\n\n**The message must be small and must not be wrong.** Two to three lines. It names the preferred path AND the one\ncase where `grep` is genuinely correct, so an agent that reads it and continues with `grep` for a string-literal\nsearch has been *helped*, not overridden. Something of the shape:\n\n```\nSerena (LSP) is available: find_referencing_symbols / find_symbol resolve real references — prefer it for\n\"who calls/imports X\". grep is still right for symbols named as STRINGS (monkeypatch.setattr, getattr) and\nfor current line numbers, which the LSP index can lag.\n```\n\n**Non-blocking, always.** The hook informs; it never denies the call.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.claude/settings.json` — the `PreToolUse` matcher on `Bash` and its command/message.\n\n## Testing\n\n- The hook fires on a plain `grep -rn foo src/` and on `rg foo`.\n- It does NOT block: the grep still runs and its output is unchanged.\n- A command with no grep produces no reminder.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a `PreToolUse` hook on `Bash` emits the reminder for `grep`, `rg`, `egrep`, `fgrep`\n- [ ] the trigger is a plain grep-family string match — no pattern classification, no path heuristics — and the\n      hook config is small enough to read at a glance\n- [ ] the message is <= 3 lines and names both `find_referencing_symbols` AND the string-literal/line-number\n      grep exceptions, so it is never misleading\n- [ ] the hook is non-blocking: a transcript shows the grep executing normally after the reminder\n- [ ] a transcript shows it firing on `grep -rn foo src/` and not firing on a non-grep command","id":"4143-9afe-6479-4244","parent_id":"9109-2ad9-2477-4cf6","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"A — PreToolUse hook: re-surface Serena on every grep call"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785368698660420001,"uuid":"ef6ec7c4-eacf-46b8-9873-0ee550e48b71"}